---
// VYGENEROVÁNO z src/pages/zpetna-vazba.astro skriptem tools/i18n/make_en.py.
// Neupravovat ručně: změny patří do tools/i18n/en/zpetna-vazba.py.
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base
  lang="en"
  title="Feedback and repeat bookings | ALSflow"
  description="After the visit the assistant asks how it went, drafts a reply to the review and invites the customer back at the right time. 2,500 CZK a month, no commitment."
  canonical="https://alsflow.cz/en/feedback"
  ogTitle="Feedback and repeat bookings"
  ogDescription="A question after the visit, a draft reply to the review and an invitation to book again. 2,500 CZK a month."
  current="/en/ai-assistants"
>
  <Fragment slot="head">
  <script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Service",
  "name": "Feedback and repeat bookings",
  "inLanguage": "en",
  "serviceType": "Automated feedback collection and repeat-visit invitations for small businesses",
  "description": "After the visit the assistant asks how it went, drafts a reply to the review and invites the customer back at the right time.",
  "areaServed": {
    "@type": "Country",
    "name": "Czech Republic"
  },
  "provider": {
    "@type": "Organization",
    "name": "ALSflow",
    "legalName": "Jakub Ryvola",
    "taxID": "30112702",
    "url": "https://alsflow.cz"
  },
  "offers": {
    "@type": "Offer",
    "price": "2500",
    "priceCurrency": "CZK",
    "priceSpecification": {
      "@type": "UnitPriceSpecification",
      "price": "2500",
      "priceCurrency": "CZK",
      "unitCode": "MON"
    }
  }
}
  </script>
  <script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How much does it cost?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "2,500 CZK a month on its own, or together with bookings and email replies for 7,500 CZK a month. One-time setup 8,000 to 10,000 CZK. No commitment, cancel any time."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Does the assistant reply to reviews on my behalf?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "No. It prepares a draft and sends it to you for approval. You can send it with one click, edit it, or throw it away. It never publishes anything under a public review without you."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Will it not annoy customers?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "It is one message after the visit and, where relevant, one invitation when the usual interval for the next visit is coming up. Whoever does not reply gets no second reminder. You set the frequency and can change it any time."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Where do the dates for the invitation come from?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "From your shared Google Calendar, just like bookings. The assistant sees when the customer was last in and suggests when to get in touch based on the usual interval."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How long does the setup take?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "5 to 7 working days from the first fifteen-minute call. I handle the connection, the texts and the testing."
      }
    }
  ]
}
  </script>
  </Fragment>

  <section class="hero hero-plain">
    <div class="aurora" aria-hidden="true"><i class="a1"></i><i class="a2"></i></div>
    <div class="wrap">
      <h1 class="h-hero fade-head reveal-words" style="max-width:16ch">Feedback and <span class="grad">repeat bookings</span></h1>
      <p class="lead">Winning a new customer costs many times more than inviting back someone who has
        already been. After the visit the assistant asks how it went, drafts a reply to the public review
        and sends an invitation for the next appointment at the right time.</p>
      <div class="btn-row">
        <a class="btn btn-grad btn-shine" href="/en/contact">Get a free quote</a>
        <a class="btn btn-quiet" href="/en/pricing">Pricing</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec sec-line scene-host" id="co-dela">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <h2 class="h-sec fade-head reveal-words">What there is <span class="grad">never time for</span></h2>
        <p class="lead">Not because it is unimportant. Because it happens after the customer has left.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rows">
        <div class="row rev"><span class="num">01</span><div><h3>A question after the visit</h3><p>A short message a day or two after the visit: was everything all right? If someone is unhappy, you are the first to know, not the last to read it in a public review.</p></div></div>
        <div class="row rev" data-d="1"><span class="num">02</span><div><h3>A draft reply to the review</h3><p>When someone leaves a rating, the assistant drafts a reply in your tone and sends it to you for approval. Send, edit, or throw away. It publishes nothing by itself.</p></div></div>
        <div class="row rev" data-d="2"><span class="num">03</span><div><h3>An invitation for the next appointment</h3><p>Based on when the customer was last in and the usual interval in your field. Not too early, and not a year later when they have found someone else.</p></div></div>
        <div class="row rev" data-d="3"><span class="num">04</span><div><h3>Monthly report</h3><p>How many people replied, how they rated you and how many came back. On one page.</p></div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec sec-dark sec-line" id="proc">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <h2 class="h-sec fade-head reveal-words">An unhappy customer <span class="grad">usually says nothing</span></h2>
        <p class="lead">They just do not come back. And when they do say something, it is often in public and you
          are the last to hear about it. A private question right after the visit gives you room to fix things before it
          becomes a rating every future customer reads. The second thing is coming back: a customer who
          left happy will return if they think of you at the moment they need that service
          again. The invitation is for exactly that moment.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec sec-line" id="jak">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <h2 class="h-sec fade-head reveal-words">How it <span class="grad">works</span></h2>
      </div>
      <div class="cards-3">
        <div class="panel panel-pad panel-glow rev">
          <h3>1. A fifteen-minute call</h3>
          <p>You tell me how often people usually come back and the tone you use with them.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="panel panel-pad panel-glow rev" data-d="1">
          <h3>2. I set it up for you</h3>
          <p>Within 5 to 7 working days I connect the calendar, prepare the message texts and test them.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="panel panel-pad panel-glow rev" data-d="2">
          <h3>3. It runs by itself</h3>
          <p>Replies to reviews come to you for approval. Everything else happens without you.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec sec-dark sec-line" id="cena">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <h2 class="h-sec fade-head reveal-words">2,500 CZK a month, <span class="grad">no commitment</span></h2>
        <p class="lead">You can have it on its own, or together with the other two assistants for
          7,500 CZK a month. One-time setup 8,000 to 10,000 CZK. Cancel any time, with no notice period.</p>
        <div class="btn-row">
          <a class="btn btn-grad btn-magnet" href="/en/contact">I want this one</a>
          <a class="btn btn-quiet" href="/en/pricing">Full pricing</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec sec-line" id="dalsi">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <h2 class="h-sec fade-head reveal-words">Other <span class="grad">assistants</span></h2>
      </div>
      <div class="cards-2">
        <a class="panel panel-pad panel-glow rev" href="/en/email-replies">
          <h3>Email replies</h3>
          <p>Reads your email, answers routine questions and passes on whatever it does not know. 2,500 CZK a month.</p>
        </a>
        <a class="panel panel-pad panel-glow rev" data-d="1" href="/en/bookings-and-reminders">
          <h3>Bookings and reminders</h3>
          <p>Books appointments into your calendar and reminds people the day before. 4,500 CZK a month.</p>
        </a>
      </div>
        <p class="lead" style="max-width:none;margin-top:1.4rem">Want to see it for your own field?
          <a href="/en/ai-assistant-for-physiotherapists">For physiotherapists</a> or
          <a href="/en/ai-assistant-for-hair-salons">for hair salons</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec sec-dark sec-line" id="faq">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <h2 class="h-sec fade-head reveal-words">Your questions</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="faq">
        <details class="rev"><summary>How much does it cost?</summary><p>2,500 CZK a month on its own, or together with bookings and email replies for 7,500 CZK a month. One-time setup 8,000 to 10,000 CZK. No commitment, cancel any time.</p></details>
        <details class="rev" data-d="1"><summary>Does the assistant reply to reviews on my behalf?</summary><p>No. It prepares a draft and sends it to you for approval. You can send it with one click, edit it, or throw it away. It never publishes anything under a public review without you.</p></details>
        <details class="rev" data-d="2"><summary>Will it not annoy customers?</summary><p>It is one message after the visit and, where relevant, one invitation when the usual interval for the next visit is coming up. Whoever does not reply gets no second reminder. You set the frequency and can change it any time.</p></details>
        <details class="rev" data-d="3"><summary>Where do the dates for the invitation come from?</summary><p>From your shared Google Calendar, just like bookings. The assistant sees when the customer was last in and suggests when to get in touch based on the usual interval.</p></details>
        <details class="rev" data-d="4"><summary>How long does the setup take?</summary><p>5 to 7 working days from the first fifteen-minute call. I handle the connection, the texts and the testing.</p></details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec">
    <div class="wrap" style="text-align:center">
      <h2 class="h-sec fade-head reveal-words">How many customers <span class="grad">never came back</span>?</h2>
      <p class="lead lead-center rev" data-d="1">A free fifteen-minute call. We go through what you need and I suggest a solution and a price.</p>
      <div class="btn-row rev" data-d="2" style="justify-content:center">
        <a class="btn btn-grad btn-shine" href="/en/contact">Get a free quote</a>
        <a class="btn btn-quiet" href="/en/ai-assistants">All assistants</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
